<newsitem itemid="17681" id="root" date="1996-08-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Astec half year pretax profit jumps 32.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Astec half year pretax profit jumps 32.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.32		   vs 2.60</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.63		   vs 0.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     13.1		   vs 9.9</p>
<p> Turnover		   199.1		  vs 174.3</p>
<p> Operating profit	 12.48		  vs 9.48</p>
<p> Interest receivable    0.62		   vs 0.44</p>
<p> Tax charge		 2.75		   vs 1.89</p>
<p> Net taxed		  10.34		  vs 8.03</p>
<p> Retained profit	  8.38		   vs 6.49</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 5</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 1</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Sept 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Astec Plc, the UK power conversion products group, said it expected its financial performance to continue to improve during the second half of 1996 in a period of lower market growth. The group added that it was committed to keeping costs under tight control.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
